B.a2Q=new A.dL("    One would be eternally grateful for the honor of\n    having met these incredible creatures.\n    ",!1)
B.a2R=new A.dL("They say to never meet your heroes.",!0)
B.a2S=new A.dL("    The dulcet tones echoed through the forest,\n    as if sang by Mother Nature herself.\n    ",!1)
B.a2T=new A.dL("No Fey could resist hearing the unmistakable call of Nature herself.",!0)
B.a2U=new A.dL("      In the event of multiple copies of [this], the one belonging to the controller\n      of the card triggering the replacement event procs first (and wins).\n    ",!0)
B.a2V=new A.dL("    Altaria was renowned for its sprawling navy; the fishing boats\n    were the backbone of the kingdom's economy.\n    ",!1)
B.a2W=new A.dL('"I am all nature; nature is but me."',!0)
B.a2X=new A.dL("    Not only was she floating in dreams like dandelions;\n    she could gather the Fey to fulfill them.\n    ",!1)
B.a2Y=new A.dL("    Scattered across the rivers and coast of Altaria there were\n    lighthouses to guide the kingdom's vessels and spirits.\n    ",!1)
B.a2Z=new A.dL('    "To thee I pledge my sword, my life, and my soul;\n    your majesty; my Queen. All hail Queen Brittany II!"\n    ',!1)
B.a3_=new A.dL('    "The Guild of Paladins still hoped that one day Theranor\n    would return to lead them." \u2014 _A Brief History of Altaria_, p. 194\n    ',!1)
B.a32=new A.dL("The hard work of many peasants keeps the kingdom of Altaria fed.",!0)
B.a33=new A.dL('    The big-lettered "FEY ONLY" on the sign had to later be prefixed with "non-transformed".\n    ',!0)
B.a34=new A.dL("    The cities of Altaria thrive under the rule of law, enforced by the royal guards of Her Majesty,\n    Queen Brittany II.\n    ",!0)
B.a36=new A.dL("    If you ignore the whispers, you might find yourself dead.\n    If you listen to them, you might find yourself mad.\n    ",!1)
B.a37=new A.dL("It was said that he could make an offer one couldn't refuse.",!0)
B.a39=new A.dL('    "They met in a tiny tree house, in which Theranor could barely fit. Luckily the atmosphere was amiable, so the\n    paladins felt comfortable doffing their bulky outfits." \u2014 _A Brief History of Altaria_, p. 34\n    ',!0)
B.a3a=new A.dL("The tips of his arrows were as sharp as his words.",!0)
B.a3b=new A.dL("It was as if the entire forest was suddenly awake. And she was _not_ happy.",!0)
B.a3c=new A.dL('    "After the Cataclysm, only Theranor\'s sword was recovered;\n    still a legendary symbol of hope for the paladins, and all Men of Altaria."\n    \u2014 _A Brief History of Altaria_, p. 169\n    ',!1)
B.a3d=new A.dL('"Let the light of Galadon shine through me, and I shall be His tool."',!0)
